      "From that night on, Flicker never wished for a bigger light again. She understood that her small glow had a special purpose — to be gentle, to be comforting, to be the kind of light that helps without overwhelming. And on every dark night after that, when small creatures were lost or afraid, they would look for one specific light — a tiny, gentle glow that whispered, 'Follow me. You are not alone.'",
      "And that tiny light was always there, flickering bravely in the darkness, proving that you don't need to be big to make a difference. You just need to shine your own unique light, however small, for those who need it most. Sleep well, little light. Your glow matters more than you know."
